**Do not make TrueCost merely better at scraping Amazon, Flipkart, Blinkit, Zomato, Uber, Ola and the other providers. Make it better than any individual provider at understanding the user's intent across all of them.**

Amazon or Flipkart knows its own catalog extremely well. Zomato understands food search extremely well. Uber understands mobility context extremely well. A comparator such as BuyHatke specializes in shopping price intelligence, while Comparify currently emphasizes groceries, food and rides. citeturn10search0turn10search10

TrueCost's opportunity is different:

> **One universal intent engine, eight domain-aware identity models, one cross-provider evidence graph, and one deterministic decision layer.**

That is the architecture I would build to move TrueCost from its current search behavior to an genuinely elite multi-category decision system.